; ------------------------------------------------------------------
; Pages for secrets (`stdlib/Crypto/Secret.ax`). A key lives in a
; private anonymous mapping of its own, outside the arena, so a region
; reset cannot reclaim it under a live handle. The mapping is locked
; so it is not written to swap, and where the kernel has an advice for
; it, left out of core dumps. Both are best effort: `Crypto.Secret`
; answers whether each one took, and a kernel that refuses (an
; `RLIMIT_MEMLOCK` of zero, say) leaves the key usable and unlocked.
; A 0 below means the target has no such call.
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
;; MAP_PRIVATE | MAP_ANONYMOUS = 0x02 | 0x20
(pub :: mapPrivateAnon Int)
(pub fn (mapPrivateAnon)
  34)

;; mlock - 149
(pub :: sysMlockNum Int)
(pub fn (sysMlockNum)
  149)

;; munlock - 150
(pub :: sysMunlockNum Int)
(pub fn (sysMunlockNum)
  150)

;; madvise - 28
